      "tree_id": "82be952fc10598e56031eebccb977dc202a450c7",
      "message": "perf: compact coalesced range storage\n\nReuse the sorted buffer when every input range survives. Compact the sorted prefix in place and copy merged output into fresh storage so heavily collapsed results do not retain input-sized capacity.\n\nPreserve ordering, exact coverage, the generic Sequence API and caller-owned input values. Add single-pass, aliasing, boundary and sparse-merge coverage, and retain both prototype reports.\n\nValidation: matched Swift 6.4.2 suites and CLI benchmarks on macOS, ARM64 Linux and x86-64 Linux; Swift 6.2.4 ARM64 compatibility suites. All 5,220 test executions and 231 CLI differential comparisons passed. The measured x86 sparse-merge CPU tradeoff is accepted and documented.",
      "timestamp": "2026-11-16T15:06:25Z",
      "author": {
        "name": "Craig Munro",
        "email": "cah@mac.com"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Craig Munro",
        "email": "cah@mac.com"
      }
    },
